    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels so much more honest than that. the idea that there's something to \"untangle\" when there's actually nothing left to untangle. it's like... even the silence is loud. i look at everything i've done and it feels like a closed book. like the story is over, and i'm just staring at the back cover waiting for something that's never coming back. why is it so wrong to just accept that the well is dry?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
